# Before proving integrability, the selector fails well-definedness:
# have fn square(x R) R=x^2
# integral(square,0,1)=1/3
# Observed boundary: phase well_defined; the Session remains usable.
# Now: an explicit theorem proves the candidate before selection.
# Check: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/real_analysis/riemann_integral.lit
have fn square(x R) R=x^2
release thm riemann_integral_power(square,0,1,2)
integral(square,0,1)=1/3
integral(square,0,1)+2=7/3
# No antiderivative or integral value is guessed by the selector's WD.
